{"name":"Seaworld","hex":"#125459","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"SeaWorld","blocks":[{"text":"SeaWorld is an American theme park chain with headquarters in Orlando, Florida. It is a proprietor of marine mammal parks, oceanariums, animal theme parks, and rehabilitation centers owned by United Parks & Resorts. The parks host shows starring marine mammals, especially dolphins and pinnipeds, as well as zoological displays featuring various other marine animals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/59/Seaworld_logo.svg/330px-Seaworld_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SeaWorld"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Shamu_with_trainer.jpg/500px-Shamu_with_trainer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Shamu_with_trainer.jpg/500px-Shamu_with_trainer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kasatka, one of SeaWorld San Diego's nine killer whales, performs during a routine Shamu Adventure show.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShamu_with_trainer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/SeaWorldORL08-04-01a.JPG/500px-SeaWorldORL08-04-01a.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/SeaWorldORL08-04-01a.JPG/500px-SeaWorldORL08-04-01a.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A trainer \"surfing\" on top of Katina, a killer whale at SeaWorld Orlando.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeaWorldORL08-04-01a.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/SeaWorldORL08-04-01b.JPG/500px-SeaWorldORL08-04-01b.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.or